   "reproduction": "unreproduced: I did not inject the failure. The mechanism is quoted from code at head instead.",
   "evidence": "src/cli/daemon.ts:7-23 at head: `integrations = await mount(factory);` sits inside the try, so if mountIntegrations rejects after `factory.land.start()` (src/integrations/index.ts:44, followed by `await toolVersions()` at :56), `integrations` is undefined and `integrations?.stop()` is a no-op. In startHttp (src/server/http.ts:719-723), a local bind failure calls `credential.release()` before rethrowing. startDaemon's catch then awaits `integrations?.stop()`, which runs land.stop() and waits for workers, so the private path is unregistered while land workers can still run. At base, main.ts mounted and started the HTTP server with no cleanup at all. The ordering gap comes from this change. Impact is limited because main().catch calls process.exit(1) (src/cli/main.ts:671-673), and land.stop() aborts in-flight controllers first."
